{"uid":"1e9891b6f9416cf7","name":"test_a_substance_remedy_becomes_one_finding_that_folds_into_a_bounded_cure_task","fullName":"tests.test_petitions#test_a_substance_remedy_becomes_one_finding_that_folds_into_a_bounded_cure_task","historyId":"011bad3b981d31aff15ddc48bb0c581e","time":{"start":1791866928962,"stop":1791866928968,"duration":6},"description":"The whole of gate 1-4 clearing, and the shape of what clears them: a\n    finding-shaped record whose `clause` is the obligation, whose `evidence`\n    carries the remedy's PREAMBLE (the text before its `Done when:` marker,\n    PRD v0.28 requirement C.1, #276) -- never the done-list criteria --\n    and whose `cured_when` is the done-list text AFTER that marker, held\n    to the same clause bound review's own `cured_when` is held to (applied\n    by construction, never truncation: gate 7 declines any entry whose\n    post-marker text overruns it instead). No `invalidates` (a remedy names\n    no invalidated evidence path, so the re-record cascade is never\n    triggered from here). The second half runs the record through the real\n    `insert_cure_tasks` to pin that the bound holds and that the full\n    preamble survives in `description`.\n\n    The `cured_when` assertions replace this node's original `assert\n    \"cured_when\" not in finding`, and inverting that pin is the point rather\n    than a relaxation (unit-3 review): with the field absent, the criterion\n    came from `state._cure_task_success_criteria`, which folds `clause`\n    BEFORE `evidence` and truncates the pair -- so an obligation that is\n    itself five clauses long consumed the whole budget and the remedy was\n    absent from the criterion ENTIRELY, leaving the task scored against the\n    exact text the worker petitioned as unmeetable. The third half below is\n    that regression, and everything the original pin was protecting -- the\n    same bound, no refusal, the full text in `description` -- is still\n    asserted, now against `plan_ingestion.clause_count_overrun` itself so\n    `petitions`' own duplicated bound cannot drift from it.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The whole of gate 1-4 clearing, and the shape of what clears them: a<br />\nfinding-shaped record whose <code>clause</code> is the obligation, whose <code>evidence</code><br />\ncarries the remedy's PREAMBLE (the text before its <code>Done when:</code> marker,<br />\nPRD v0.28 requirement C.1, #276) -- never the done-list criteria --<br />\nand whose <code>cured_when</code> is the done-list text AFTER that marker, held<br />\nto the same clause bound review's own <code>cured_when</code> is held to (applied<br />\nby construction, never truncation: gate 7 declines any entry whose<br />\npost-marker text overruns it instead). No <code>invalidates</code> (a remedy names<br />\nno invalidated evidence path, so the re-record cascade is never<br />\ntriggered from here). The second half runs the record through the real<br />\n<code>insert_cure_tasks</code> to pin that the bound holds and that the full<br />\npreamble survives in <code>description</code>.</p>\n<pre><code>The `cured_when` assertions replace this node's original `assert\n&quot;cured_when&quot; not in finding`, and inverting that pin is the point rather\nthan a relaxation (unit-3 review): with the field absent, the criterion\ncame from `state._cure_task_success_criteria`, which folds `clause`\nBEFORE `evidence` and truncates the pair -- so an obligation that is\nitself five clauses long consumed the whole budget and the remedy was\nabsent from the criterion ENTIRELY, leaving the task scored against the\nexact text the worker petitioned as unmeetable. The third half below is\nthat regression, and everything the original pin was protecting -- the\nsame bound, no refusal, the full text in `description` -- is still\nasserted, now against `plan_ingestion.clause_count_overrun` itself so\n`petitions`' own duplicated bound cannot drift from it.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":fals